atlas 1

// Rosetta's design intent: what the code cannot say about itself, graded against the code by Project Atlas.
// Crate roots and a few seams carry their own `@atlas` lines (`grep -rn '@atlas' crates clients`).
// Duties and the one command: CLAUDE.md "Atlas"; the authoring guide is the `atlas` skill.

system rosetta "Rosetta" {
  intent "Multi-agent ingestion engine: ledger every raw record coding agents write, serve one canonical projection over localhost HTTP/WS."
  thesis """
    Three jobs, in consumer priority: search, observe, monitor.
    L1 ground truth → L2 runtime → L3 services: data flows up, dependencies point down.
    All knowledge of one agent lives in its pair: groundtruth/<agent> and crates/adapters/<agent>.
    Two data representations only: an append-only raw ledger and one disposable projection, rebuilt, never migrated.
    Parsers exist once, in Rust; consumers get generated types and dial the daemon, never the store.
    """
  see "CLAUDE.md#iron-rules-each-one-is-a-spaghetti-failure-mode--do-not-relitigate"
  see "docs/ARCHITECTURE.md#rosetta-architecture"
}

// The adapter glob also matches rosetta-adapter-support; the agents are the other 9.
let $agents = crate:rosetta-adapter-*, !crate:rosetta-adapter-support
